<http://data.silknow.org/event/f28c03b8-1cdf-3a49-b818-76096e10d12d>
        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Formerly part of the Castle Howard Costume collection, the private collection of George Howard.  Purchased on 7 October 2003 from the Sotheby's.\n\nHistorical significance: An unusual example of a banyan or nightgown for a woman.  It combines the T-shape of a man's nightgown inspired by the Japanese kimono with the traditional shaping at the back and sides for a woman's gown.  This would have been worn informally in the privacy of home."@en ;
        ecrm:P14_carried_out_by        <http://data.silknow.org/actor/9041b597-af7a-3cdd-9b24-9b52e2f112bf> ;
