        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Formerly part of the Castle Howard Costume collection, the private collection of George Howard.  Purchased on 7 October 2003 from the Sotheby's.\n\nHistorical significance: An unusual example of a banyan or nightgown for a woman.  It combines the T-shape of a man's nightgown inspired by the Japanese kimono with the traditional shaping at the back and sides for a woman's gown.  This would have been worn informally in the privacy of home."@en .

